# P2-sound lane log (append-only)

## 2026-10-16 — lane/sound kickoff: stack selection

Divergence under fix: our TUI mirrors sound playback to a system player
(detached `spawn`: pw-play/paplay/ffplay/mpv/canberra), while v2 plays
in-process through miniaudio (opentui `@opentui/core` Audio → native Zig
engine → vendored miniaudio 0.11.22).

### Candidate evaluation (all evidence local + crates.io sparse index)

1. **cpal 0.18.x / rodio 0.20.x — REJECTED.** cpal's Linux host is a
   link-time dependency: `alsa`/`alsa-sys` emit `cargo:rustc-link-lib=asound`
   (cpal 0.18 additionally pulls `jack`, `pipewire`, `pulseaudio` sys crates —
   every one a native dev-header link). This box has only `libasound.so.2`
   (no `libasound.so` dev symlink; `ld -lasound` fails) and CI
   (.github/workflows/ci.yml, `ubuntu-latest`) runs no `apt-get`, so cpal
   needs a CI workflow change + dev packages — incompatible with "dependency
   tree stays compatible with the workspace and the 20-min CI build", and it
   would add a hard link-time ALSA dep to every binary.
2. **crates.io `miniaudio` 0.10.0 (→ `ep-miniaudio-sys` 2.4.0) — REJECTED.**
   Vendored C is right (dlopen ALSA/Pulse at runtime, no link-time deps), but
   the sys crate runs **bindgen 0.54 at build time**, which panics on modern
   glibc headers (`__atomic_wide_counter_struct_... is not a valid Ident`,
   reproduced locally: bindgen-0.54.0/src/ir/context.rs:894) and requires
   libclang discovery at build time. Dead on this toolchain (rustc 1.99) and
   on ubuntu-latest.
3. **Vendored miniaudio sys crate with pre-generated bindings — CHOSEN.**
   Mirrors the repo's third_party convention (agent-client-protocol,
   tree-sitter-toml) AND is byte-for-byte the engine v2 uses:
   `third_party/opentui/packages/native/src/vendor/miniaudio/miniaudio.h`
   (miniaudio 0.11.22, copied verbatim into `third_party/miniaudio-sys/`)
   + the same shim flags opentui compiles it with on Linux
   (`miniaudio_shim.c`: `MA_ENABLE_ONLY_SPECIFIC_BACKENDS` +
   `MA_ENABLE_ALSA` + `MA_ENABLE_PULSEAUDIO` — runtime `dlopen`, no null
   backend). Bindings are pre-generated once with bindgen 0.70 and committed
   (`src/bindings.rs`), so builds need only `cc` — no bindgen, no libclang,
   no system dev headers, no network. Dep-tree delta: **1 path-only crate +
   `cc` (already in the lock via tree-sitter)**.

### v2 parity facts (citations)

- `packages/tui/src/audio.ts:7-21` — `Audio.create({autoStart:false})` in a
  try/catch; on failure `audio = null` and every later `loadSoundFile`/`play`
  is a silent no-op returning null/false.
- `packages/tui/src/audio.ts:38-43` — `play()`: if not started and
  `start()` fails → null (the candidate loop in `attention.ts:110-126` then
  gives up → `sound=false`).
- `packages/tui/src/attention.ts:65-76` — volume clamp 0..1 (`clampVolume`);
  native clamps again to 0..4 (`audio.zig`: `clamp(options.volume, 0, 4)`).
- Engine: `audio.zig` `createEngine` — `ma_engine_init` with
  `noDevice = MA_TRUE` (pure mixer; succeeds headless), device
  `ma_device_init`+`ma_device_start` lazily at `audioStart`
  (`ma_device_config_init(ma_device_type_playback)`, callback →
  `ma_engine_read_pcm_frames`).
- Decode: `audio.zig` `decodeSoundFromMemory` —
  `ma_decoder_config_init(ma_format_f32, 0, 0)` (f32, native channels/rate)
  → `ma_decoder_init_memory` → read all frames → cached `Sound { channels,
  sample_rate, samples: []f32 }` (TUI caches per file path,
  `audio.ts:23-36`).
- Play: `audio.zig` `audioPlay` — `ma_audio_buffer_ref_init(f32, channels,
  samples, frames)` (sampleRate patched) → `ma_sound_init_from_data_source(
  engine, &buffer_ref, MA_SOUND_FLAG_NO_SPATIALIZATION | MA_SOUND_FLAG_NO_PITCH,
  group)` → `ma_sound_set_volume(clamp(v,0,4))` → `ma_sound_start`; finished
  voices reaped on later calls.
- No env kill-switch exists in v2's audio path (only the
  `config.attention.sound` boolean + per-request `sound:false`,
  `attention.ts:70-76`); the only env var is `OPENCODE_NODE_ASSETS_DIR` for
  node-build asset *paths* (`attention-sounds.node.ts:7-8`). Port keeps the
  existing config gate and adds no new env var.

### Plan

1. `third_party/miniaudio-sys`: header + shim + pre-generated bindings + cc
   build.rs (link dl/pthread/m on unix).
2. oc-tui: in-process `InprocSoundPlayer` (engine/no-device mixer, lazy
   device, decode cache, voice mixer) behind `cfg(target_os = "linux")`;
   non-Linux keeps the process-player fallback. Trigger matrix untouched.
3. Tests: per-asset decode sanity, bogus-device graceful no-op, existing
   trigger tests stay green; fmt/clippy/nextest/release size delta.

## 2026-10-16 — implementation + verification results

### Deliverables

- `third_party/miniaudio-sys/` — vendored miniaudio 0.11.22 (header copied
  byte-identical from opentui's native vendor dir), shim with v2's Linux
  backend selection (ALSA+Pulse only, runtime dlopen, no null backend),
  pre-generated bindings.rs (bindgen 0.70, allow-listed surface), cc-only
  build.rs linking just dl/pthread/m.
- `crates/oc-tui/src/sound/inproc.rs` — the port of v2's engine:
  no-device `ma_engine` mixer (created once per process), lazy
  `ma_device_init`+`ma_device_start` retried per play (v2 latches
  `playbackStarted` only on success), path-keyed decode cache
  (`ma_decoder_config_init(f32, 0, 0)` → read-all), playback via
  `ma_audio_buffer_ref_init` + sampleRate patch +
  `ma_sound_init_from_data_source(NO_SPATIALIZATION|NO_PITCH)` +
  `ma_sound_set_volume(clamp 0..4)` + `ma_sound_start`, voice reap on
  `ma_sound_at_end`, MAX_VOICES=64 cap (v2's pool guard). Every failure =
  `false` (silent no-op); no process spawn anywhere.
- `crates/oc-tui/src/sound.rs` — `SoundHalf` alias: in-process player on
  Linux, the spawn mirror (`ProcessSoundPlayer`/`PlayerKind`) kept for
  other targets and its argv tests stay green everywhere.
- `crates/oc-tui/src/app.rs` — the run loop installs
  `sound::SoundHalf::default()`; trigger matrix untouched (store/
  notifications_plugin trigger tests all green).
- Kill-switch: none added — v2 has no env kill-switch for audio (cited in
  the kickoff entry); the existing `config.attention.sound` +
  per-request gates already mirror v2.

### Dependency-size impact

- Dep-tree delta: +1 path-only crate (`miniaudio-sys`); its only build
  dep `cc` was already in Cargo.lock (tree-sitter). Cargo.lock unchanged.
- Release binary: 68,145,760 B (main baseline) → 68,671,744 B =
  **+525,984 B (+0.77%)** — the miniaudio engine + dr_mp3 decoder.
- Build time: miniaudio-sys alone compiles in ~8.9 s (release, gated);
  release `-p oc-cli` 1m43s incremental; no new system deps.
- `ldd` on the release binary: no libasound/libpulse NEEDED entries —
  ALSA/Pulse are dlopen'd at runtime exactly like v2's native lib.

### Tests (all via dev-gate)

- New: `decodes_every_builtin_asset` (5 assets × format/channels/rate/
  duration sanity through the production decode path),
  `assets_keep_mp3_magic` (embedding tripwire), `bogus_sink_is_a_silent_no_op`
  (nonexistent playback sink → false ×2 incl. the retry path, no panic, no
  spawn), `undecodable_input_is_none`, `candidate_loop_gives_up_gracefully`.
- Existing sound tests: all green (argv mapping, extraction, trigger
  matrix in store/notifications_plugin).
- Gates: `cargo fmt --check` clean; `cargo clippy -p miniaudio-sys -p
  oc-tui --all-targets` clean (0 warnings);
  `cargo nextest -p oc-tui`: 666 passed / 1 skipped;
  `cargo nextest -p oc-cli`: 184 passed / 1 skipped;
  `cargo check --workspace --all-targets`: clean.
